Description
Press F10, or D-pad down, to turn the car engine off and on.

Installation instructions
1. Install ViGEmBus and HidHide, then restart Windows.
2. Unzip this folder anywhere. It does not need to be in Program Files.
3. In Steam, right-click Forza Horizon 6, open Properties, then Controller, and choose Disable Steam Input.
4. In the game, open Settings, HUD and Gameplay. Set Data Out to On, the IP address to 127.0.0.1, and the port to 5300.
5. Run FH6EngineToggle.exe, or just start the game. A watcher opens the tool whenever Forza Horizon 6 starts.

The first time only, calibrate the Cars volume when the tool asks, then do the one-time Shifting setup. After that it finds both on its own.

Windows SmartScreen may warn about the exe because it is not code-signed. Choose More info, then Run anyway.

Main features
Engine off
- The car sound fades out with a soft click and shudder.
- Accelerate is cut on the keyboard and on the controller right trigger.
- While the car is still rolling, the brakes stay on at least 5% and you can brake harder.
- Once the car is nearly stopped, the handbrake is held, so it cannot drive or reverse.
- Steering and every other button keep working.

Engine on
- A key click plays, then that car's own startup sound.
- The engine revs to 75% of its max revs, then drops straight back down. The brake and handbrake are held during the rev and released once the revs fall.
- If you drive Automatic, the tool switches to Manual for the rev so the brake does not reverse the car, then switches back.

Press F10, or D-pad down while driving, to toggle. Close the tool or quit the game to stop. Either way, the tool hands the controller back.

Requirements
- Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit
- Forza Horizon 6 on Steam
- ViGEmBus, for the startup rev, the minimum brake, and the parking hold
- HidHide, to cut the controller triggers while the engine is off

Without those drivers, the tool still mutes and unmutes the car sound, and it shows what is missing when it starts.

No game files are included.

Shout outs
vgmstream, vgamepad, ViGEm, and PyInstaller.
